{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Deeds"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Personal Heroes"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Should Have, Ought to Have for Obligation and Recommendation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to talk about something that didn't happen in the past and that you are sorry that it didn't happen, you can use <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> or <span class=\"italic\">ought to have</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">should have</span>/<span class=\"italic\">ought to have </span>+ past participle</span> to indicate some regret or criticism about past actions, events or situations and to talk about obligations that were unfulfilled."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">should have waited</span> for the snow to stop. </span>(I'm sorry we didn't)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">ought to have been</span> more sensitive about the matter.</span> (I regret that I wasn't) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have been</span> so hasty in your decision.</span> (Criticism) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">They <span class=\"strong\">should have called</span> to let you know they weren't coming.</span> (Past obligation)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I guess I should have thought a little longer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I ought to have added that not only is he a hero, but also an inspiration. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Black people ought to have had equal rights with white people, but they didn't."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Black people's lives should have been better."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There were many discriminatory laws that should have changed sooner."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Uses of the First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">First Conditional</span> to talk about events or situations that are likely to happen. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "To be precise about the certainty or nature of the event taking place, you can choose to use a variety of modal verbs such as:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">will</span> (99% certain)</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">If we invite Joe, he<span class=\"strong\">'ll</span> be really happy. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">can</span> (ability)</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">If I go too, I <span class=\"strong\">can</span> give you a ride.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">going to</span> (intention)</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">If I see her, I<span class=\"strong\">'m going to</span> give her a big hug.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">must</span> (necessity)</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">If you go on a vacation, you <span class=\"strong\">must</span> have a valid passport.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you don't know about Martin Luther King, Jr. you can find lots of information about him on the internet."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He believed that if you use violence to express yourself, you will cause more violence."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If people fear change and unfamiliar situations, they may react in an extreme way."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we remember Martin Luther King, Jr.'s vision and bravery, we will work toward a more peaceful future for all people."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hero "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person admired for their achievements"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Someone recently asked me who a personal hero of mine was."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about social issues."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "discriminatory "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "showing prejudice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There were many discriminatory laws that should have changed sooner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "racial segregation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dividing people by race"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He fought against racial segregation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le13ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "violence "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "behavior 