"Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": ""}, {"time": "100", "text": "I've been thinking a lot about inequality and injustice. Someone recently asked me who a personal hero of mine was. I guess I should have thought a little longer, but I immediately answered, Martin Luther King, Jr. I ought to have added that not only is he a hero, but also an inspiration. If you don't know about Martin Luther King, Jr. you can find lots of information about him on the internet.\nDr. Martin Luther King, Jr. was born in Atlanta, Georgia in the United States in 1929. At that time in America, black people ought to have had equal rights with white people, but they didn't. Black people had to sit in the back of buses. The schools were segregated and there were even separate public restrooms for black people and white people. Black people's lives should have been better.", "id": 1, "image": ""}, {"time": "45000", "text": "Martin Luther King, Jr. was a minister in the Baptist Church. He fought against racial segregation. He wanted equal rights for all people, but he didn't use violence in his fight. He believed that if you use violence to express yourself, you will cause more violence. He asked people to fight peacefully. For example, he asked black people to ride in the front of the bus. More than 200,000 people went to Washington D.C. to listen to him speak and ask the government to change unfair laws. There were many discriminatory laws that should have changed sooner.", "id": 2, "image": ""}, {"time": "81000", "text": "Because of Martin Luther King, Jr., many laws began to change in the United States. However, many white people disagreed with him and his ways. If people fear change and unfamiliar situations, they may react in an extreme way. In 1968, Martin Luther King, Jr. was assassinated by a white man.<br/>\nEvery year, on the third Monday of January, Americans remember Martin Luther King, Jr. They try to remember how much America has changed and they think about how much more America should change in the future. If we remember Martin Luther King, Jr.'s vision and bravery, we will work toward a more peaceful future for all people.", "id": 3, "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn11le13ob03re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": [], "title": ""}]}]}